WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:05.467
-Welcome back. We are here
with Lewis Black right now.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:06.934
Lewis, you're a great comedian

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.400
who's known
for your strong opinions

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.267
about all kinds
of different topics.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.100
So with that in mind,
it's time to play a game we call

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.467
"Wheel of Opinions."

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.868
Here we go.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:18.267
-♪ Wheel of Opinions ♪

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.534
-Now, here's how it works.
I'm gonna hit this button here,

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.067
which will activate
an opinion topic generator.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.934
-Okay.
-It'll land on a random topic,

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:27.300
and whatever it is, you just
give your opinion on it.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.834
-No problem.
-Here we go.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.567
Let's do this.
Here we go.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:34.367
[ Beeping ]

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.067
-Oh, cooking for yourself.

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:39.601
That's -- Look.
You don't cook for yourself!

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.901
Okay? Because that's
the road to insanity.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.934
-Wow.
-I'll tell you why.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:50.801
-Yeah.
-Fractions.

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.434
Okay?

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:56.634
Any recipe is for a family --
a nice family of four,

00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:00.501
not for some miserable
aging prick.

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:05.400
You got to take 1/16th
of a thing of cumin?

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.667
That's not -- That's not a --
That's a formula for a stroke.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.100
-Too much math. Too much math.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.634
Here we go.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.434
-Who wrote the music?

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.200
Oh. Vaccines.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.534
-[ Audience "oohs" ]
-Oh. "Ooh!" "Ohh!"

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:29.834
I'll tell you this.
I've been triple vaxxed.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:34.534
If I can fill my bathtub
every day with the vaccine,

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:35.868
I'd hop right in it.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:39.534
I would -- I would wash myself
in the vaccine.

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:41.567
I got no problem with it.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.767
Look. We live in a country --

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.801
I don't understand
why people don't do it.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.501
They're taking supplements.
We'd scarf them down.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.133
We spend billions of dollars.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.601
We eat them -- We eat
supplements like they're candy.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:55.234
CBD oil, for God's sake.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:58.734
It comes from a weed
at the side of the road!

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:01.267
And people are like,
"Oh, chuggy, chug, chug."

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.701
I take something
called ashwagandha.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.367
It's an herb
that comes from India.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.701
It's supposed to calm you down.
Doing a great job!

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.801
[ Ding ]

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.334
-Oh, my God.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.467
Let's get --

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.367
[ Beeping ]

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.133
-Oh. Bean bag chairs.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:30.334
If you buy a bean bag chair,
something is so wrong with you.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:35.133
Why would --
It's a bean bag chair.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:39.067
You don't -- You cook beans.
You don't sit on beans.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.834
Okay?
-God.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:43.300
-When I was in college --
and we were doing a lot --

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.334
I was doing a ton of pot,
just tons of it.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.167
And I'd sit --
You'd sit on a bean bag chair.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.868
You never thought,
"Oh, I'm comfortable."

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.701
What you thought was,
"I'm gonna get a knife,

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:52.868
I'm going to open this up,

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:54.400
I'm gonna make
some [bleep] dinner."

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:03.267
-I don't know if I can take it.
I'm going to have a stroke.

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.367
Okay.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.968
[ Beeping ]

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.901
-QAnon. Oh, yeah.
Another good group.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.667
They recently,
a while back there,

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:18.067
they decided they're going to
go to Dealey Plaza,

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:20.634
which is where Kennedy was shot.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:23.367
And they went there,
a bunch of them,

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:26.133
because they were gathering
to meet up with --

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.567
John F. Kennedy Jr.
Was going to show up.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:31.901
And then they were
going to go with him,

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.534
and John F. Kennedy Jr.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:36.067
was going to show up
with our former leader,

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:38.067
and then they were going to go
to the White House,

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:41.501
and then they were gonna tell
the President to leave,

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:43.400
and he would, of course, leave.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.901
And...

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.267
And, uh --
-Yeah.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:49.100
-I -- What's -- It's --
[ Stammering ]

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.667
How -- How crazy do you
have to be to think that?

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:56.934
I had called John Kennedy Jr.
the day before,

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.934
and he said, "I'm not coming."

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.834
-[ Laughter ]
-He answered the phone?

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.767
And he said, "There's no way
I'm going to come to that."

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.167
-He said, "No."

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:07.267
-He said, "There's no way
I'm going to do that."

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.467
[ Beeping ]

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.834
-Oh, here we go.
-This music is spectacular.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.000
-Thank you. I wrote it
on my phone, believe it or not.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.334
Oh, social media.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:19.734
-Social media, which goes back
pretty much to QAnon.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.801
We can combine those two
in a way.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:25.200
Because I have such a joy
about social media.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.534
What -- I've learned one thing
from social media,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:32.334
and QAnon kind of proves
what I'm going to say,

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.033
and that is this --

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:37.868
if you make something up

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:45.033
and then you believe
what you made up is true...

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:47.834
then you are crazy.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:55.400
And -- And if you read something
that someone had made up

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.501
and you believe what they made
up is true, you're crazier.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:01.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.801
[ Bell dings ]
-That is Lewis Black!

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:07.100
Lewis Black.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.367
Lewisblack.com.
Anything Lewis Black.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.934
Catch him live on
his "Off the Rails" tour.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.968
Check out his latest special,
"Thanks for Risking Your Life."

